     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.25\">¼ tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Fine salt"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Heat oil in a <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"24\" data-b=\"26\" data-s=\"0\">24–26 cm</span> frying pan over medium-high heat.</li><li>Lay fillets <b>skin-side down</b> away from you.</li><li>Press gently with a fish spatula for 20 seconds, then leave for 3–5 minutes until the skin releases and the flesh is opaque most of the way up.</li><li>Lower heat if the skin darkens too fast.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-high",
    "label_html": "<span>medium-high</span>",
    "off": false
   },
